IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-s150-definitions`

-- Tests for s 150. Expected values are written from the text of s 150 before the run: each definition says "includes", so a named case is JUST TRUE and any other is NOTHING.

§ `s 150 guardian includes any person who has in law or in fact the custody or control of another person`
-- (in law, in fact)
#ASSERT `s 150 guardian` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- in law only: named
#ASSERT `s 150 guardian` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- in fact only: named ("in law or in fact")
#ASSERT `s 150 guardian` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- both
#ASSERT `s 150 guardian` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING       -- neither: "includes" leaves the list open, so not covered (not "not a guardian")

§ `s 150 public place includes any place to which the public have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied`
-- (as of right, express invitation, implied invitation)
#ASSERT `s 150 public place` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 public place` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 public place` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 public place` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 public place` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a private place the public cannot enter: not covered

§ `s 150 sexual organs includes genital organs, breasts that are or appear to be female breasts and the anal region`
#ASSERT `s 150 sexual organs` `s 150 genital organs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 sexual organs` `s 150 breasts that are female breasts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 sexual organs` `s 150 breasts that appear to be female breasts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 sexual organs` `s 150 the anal region` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 sexual organs` `s 150 a part of the body that is none of those` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is open ("includes")

§ `s 150 theatre includes any place that is open to the public where entertainments are given, whether or not any charge is made for admission`
-- (open to the public, entertainments are given)
#ASSERT `s 150 theatre` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 150 theatre` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- open to the public but no entertainments are given: not covered
#ASSERT `s 150 theatre` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- entertainments but not open to the public: not covered
#ASSERT `s 150 theatre` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
